<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_Warcasket_Controller (VFEP v4.03,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml), the tier's computing-heavy set; fields not
    discussed here are the Controller's. Docs/Research/VFEP_WARCASKET_STATS.md tabulates the
    sets it sits beside.

    Tuning. The set is designed against vanilla: VFEP's 10th-generation chassis (Siegebreaker,
    Guardian, Controller, Sarcophagus, Brute are the reference numbers) carrying what Biotech's
    top mechanitor gear carries, the mechlord helmet and suit (MechBandwidth 12 each,
    ShootingAccuracyPawn -5 and MeleeHitChance -0.5 each; the suit Plasteel 120,
    ComponentSpacer 8, NanostructuringChip 2, PowerfocusChip 1; both UltraMechtech), whose
    slots the helmet and this shell take. The resurrection is at or past the top of what
    vanilla and VFEP offer, so the set is gated and priced as vanilla's top tier is:
    - researchPrerequisites VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets and UltraMechtech on all three pieces
      (BuildableDef.IsResearchFinished, which VFEP's foundry lists by, wants every entry).
      UltraMechtech needs a NanostructuringChip analyzed, so the set comes after the first
      apocriton, whose ability the core copies.
    - MechBandwidth 8 here and 12 on the helmet, 20 against the mechlord pair's 24: the shell
      pays the suit's chips for two thirds of its bandwidth and the core.
    - PsychicSensitivity -0.5, the Controller's armor's and the tier's. The helmet carries
      none (its header has why a mechanitor's suit cannot deafen its pilot), so the set leaves
      a baseline pilot at 50% where the tier's sets leave none. A psychically dull pilot
      (-0.5 of their own) reaches zero and can take no mechlink while suited.
    - The helmet alone carries the aim penalty (its header); the shoulders the command range,
      a control group and hacking speed (theirs).
    - Sharp 2 / Blunt 1 / Heat 1 on all three pieces, the tier's shared values. Blunt 1.5 is
      Guardian's and Brute's, paid for in plasteel; this set has no claim to it.
    - EnergyShieldEnergyMax 1.5 at EnergyShieldRechargeRate 0.01, the tier's baseline
      (Guardian, Controller, Sarcophagus); Siegebreaker's 2.5 and Brute's 5.0 are their
      specialties. The bubble blocks ranged fire only.
    - costList ComponentSpacer 8 / Plasteel 150 / Uranium 50 / NanostructuringChip 2 /
      PowerfocusChip 1: the plasteel and uranium are the utility sets' band (145 to 150); the
      components and chips are the mechlord suit's, the components sitting inside VFEP's
      tech-complexity dial (the utility sets 6, Controller 12, Brute 4). Set-wide that is three
      NanostructuringChips, two PowerfocusChips and two SignalChips, seven kills spread over
      the apocriton, the war queen and the diabolus, against the mechlord pair's four and one,
      which ask the apocriton four times. This piece keeps the suit's chips whole because the
      core is the apocriton's; the helmet and shoulders carry the spread (their headers).
      Parts are untradeable and destroyed on drop, so market value, the chips'
      1500 and 1000 each included, is colony wealth and raid points only.

    Alpha Mechs (sarg.alphamechs, Workshop 2973169158) leaves the tuning above standing and
    gets no compat root. It numbers the three vanilla chips tiers 1 to 3 and adds tiers 4 to 6
    behind three bosses of its own, all past UltraMechtech; the tier in each chip's label
    aside, it changes neither the mechlord pair nor any def or method this set reads, so the
    set is its tier 3 gear, tuned against the same pair as without it. Its Mech Master warcasket (VFEP_Warcasket_MechController with
    its shoulders and helmet, in its VFEP root) is the tier 6 counterpart rather than a peer:
    one chip a piece from the infernus, the war empress and the apoptosis, for MechBandwidth
    48, a 2.5 shield at twice the recharge, Blunt 1.5, a pilot who keeps most work at
    WorkSpeedGlobal -0.6 and a helmet ability that turns a hostile mech for a day. In
    ordinary materials it is the cheaper set (ComponentSpacer 7 and three chips against 16 and
    seven), so pricing this set beside it could only mean its bosses, which would move the
    apocriton's ability, tier 3 in its numbering, to tier 6. The pieces mix at the foundry as
    any VFEP sets do: this armor and helmet under its shoulders read MechBandwidth 44 with the
    core kept.

    apparel tags: WarcasketVeteran (VFEP's 10th-gen tag) puts the set on the veteran raid
    pawnkinds of both VFEP factions and Odyssey's VFEP_Salvager_Warcasket; WarcasketAll is
    VFEP_General. Threat and flavor only: AI pawns never cast apparel abilities, so a raider
    in the set is a Controller with the baseline shield and no drones.

    Resurrect mech: VEF CompAbilitiesApparel grants OLWC_ResurrectMech (AbilityDefs/
    ResurrectMech.xml), fed by the resurrection core beside it. The ability reads the core off
    the apparel that grants it, so both comps must sit on this one def. The core is
    OverlordWarcasket.CompProperties_ResurrectionCore (Source/1.6/Comps/), vanilla's
    CompProperties_ApparelReloadable with a recharge of its own, whose props class sets the
    compClass, so none is declared here. It declares no verbs, so vanilla draws no command for
    it. The core starts full, vanilla's first fill. CompDevResetCooldowns is a dev-mode cooldown
    reset for the ability (Toxin's idiom) and ships nothing in play.

    The core's numbers, all three mod settings defaulting to these values:
    - maxCharges 10, the charges held when full: the apocriton holds 30, a suit of armor a
      third. With the costs of 1 / 3 / 5 / 8 that is two heavy mechs, three medium and a
      light, or an ultraheavy and two light, in one fight, and the capacity is what limits a
      fight.
    - chargesPerDay 1, the recharge: the main supply, free and unattended. Measured against the
      vanilla route it competes with, the mech gestator's resurrect bills (Biotech/Defs/
      RecipeDefs/Recipes_MechResurrection.xml: 25 / 50 / 100 / 150 steel and one gestation
      cycle of two days for a light, medium, heavy or ultraheavy mech, any corpse age, fully
      healed), a charge a day pays for a light mech in one day, a medium in three, a heavy in
      five and an ultraheavy in eight: quicker than the gestator for a light mech and slower
      for the rest, so the gestator keeps its place and
      what the core adds is the mech back on its feet during the fight. The rate is meant to
      bring a core spent in one raid most of the way back by the next; whether that is too
      generous is an open entry in TODOs.md.
    - ammoDef ComponentSpacer at ammoCountPerCharge 1, the reload: the costly shortcut for the
      raid that follows too soon or the fight that outlasts ten charges. The item is the
      Controller's, which this set is templated from (VFEP_Warcasket_Controller reloads its
      drones with one advanced component a deployment), where vanilla's own reloadables take
      chemfuel, steel or bioferrite. At 200 silver and a fabrication bench's work each, a heavy
      mech brought back on components costs about five times its gestator bill and an
      ultraheavy about five times its own, so components stay the exception.
      Per charge rather than ammoCountToRefill, so a part-empty core
      reloads for what it lacks. baseReloadTicks, soundReload and chargeNoun are the family's
      values (the Medic's suite); chargeNoun is vanilla's default, spelled out because the
      stat sheet and the gauge's tooltip print it.
    A pilot never fetches components unasked: the gauge's drag handle sets the level an
    automatic reload fills to and starts at zero (CompResurrectionCore's header has the three
    ways a reload happens).
    - autoReloadFromInventory false: an automatic reload fetches from the map and leaves the
      components the pilot carries to the load button, as vanilla's reload never looks in an
      inventory and a carried stock reads as the player's reserve. A mod setting defaulting to
      this value. The Combat Extended root turns it on, CE's players carrying their reload
      ammo to have it used (1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ResurrectionCore.xml).

    Core sparks: OverlordWarcasket.CompProperties_CoreSparks plays OLWC_CoreSparks (Effects/
    CoreSparks.xml), the apocriton's idle red crackle, on the wearer while the core holds a
    charge and the wearer is alive, not downed and awake (CompCoreSparks' header).
    onlyWhileDrafted true also requires a player's pilot to be drafted and able to cast (a
    mechanitor while the ability's requireMechlink holds), so the crackle reads as the core
    readied for battle rather than the apocriton's constant hum; an AI pilot
    has no draft to wait on and shows it on the charge alone, as the apocriton does, until AI
    casting gives raiders a reason to spend charges. false plays it whenever the core is
    charged. A mod setting defaulting to this value. The comp reads the core off this
    def, so it sits beside it.

    Art: Textures/Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/, laid out as VFEP's sets are.
    The worn graphic is Graphic_Multi (the _north/_east/_south facings); the item icon is the
    parent's Graphic_Single, read from the bare-named file, which is a copy of the _south
    facing. No mask on the shell or the shoulders: as VFEP's Controller, the CompColorable
    colour paints the whole piece. The helmet alone carries masks; see its header.

    Own trait on equip: traitsOnEquip grants OLWC_WarcasketTrait_Overlord (TraitDefs/
    WarcasketTrait_Overlord.xml), not VFEP_WarcasketTrait, because the Overlord's work profile
    must differ from VFEP's (Research and Smithing open) and a child ApparelExtension can only
    add to what a granted trait blocks, never subtract; the trait is mirrored from VFEP's at
    startup so the patch mods that reshape VFEP's profile reshape ours. traitsOnUnequip keeps
    VFEP_Shellcasket,
    the shared "cut out of a warcasket" state every add-on set uses, so removal surgery and
    re-entombing in any warcasket behave as for VFEP's own sets.

    ApparelExtension priority 1: VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase carries its own ApparelExtension and
    inheritance appends list items, so this def resolves with two. VEF merges duplicate
    extensions in a Def.ResolveReferences prefix, highest priority surviving, and
    ApparelExtension.Merge does not copy every field; at equal priority the parent's copy
    would win. At priority 1 every field of ours, from any load root, is kept. Any new
    ApparelExtension field for this piece goes on this entry.

    Compat patches reach this def from 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml (EVA tag, cold insulation),
    1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/VacuumResistance.xml and the
    1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root (plating on CE's scale, bulk, carry capacity,
    shield, costs); see their headers.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase">
    <defName>OLWC_Warcasket_Overlord</defName>
    <label>overlord warcasket</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket shell with standard protection, equipped with a mechanoid resurrection core that can bring recently killed mechs back to life.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket shell with standard protection, equipped with a mechanoid resurrection core that can bring recently killed mechs back to life.\n\nA 10th-generation design from the government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The Overlord was its rig for veteran mechanitors, who would command their own mechs in the field rather than join a squad.\n\nThe Overlord series is meant for a mechanitor who goes into battle alone, with only their mechs beside them. The core in the shell holds only a few charges and regains them slowly, so they are best saved for the mechs that matter most. When a fight cannot wait, it can be reloaded with advanced components. The helmet greatly increases the pilot's bandwidth at some cost to their aim, the shoulders carry command relays that reach mechs anywhere on the map, and the arms are left free for smithing and hacking. Because the plating is far tougher than a mechanitor's usual armor, the pilot can lead from the front line rather than from behind the mechs.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlord</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>50</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>80</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>80</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
      <EnergyShieldRechargeRate>0.01</EnergyShieldRechargeRate>
      <EnergyShieldEnergyMax>1.5</EnergyShieldEnergyMax>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MechBandwidth>8</MechBandwidth>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.3</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.2</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>8</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>150</Plasteel>
      <Uranium>50</Uranium>
      <NanostructuringChip>2</NanostructuringChip>
      <PowerfocusChip>1</PowerfocusChip>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
      <li>UltraMechtech</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
        <li>Feet</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlord</wornGraphicPath>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="OverlordWarcasket.CompProperties_ResurrectionCore">
        <maxCharges>10</maxCharges>
        <chargesPerDay>1</chargesPerDay>
        <ammoDef>ComponentSpacer</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>1</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <autoReloadFromInventory>false</autoReloadFromInventory>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <chargeNoun>charge</chargeNoun>
      </li>
      <li Class="OverlordWarcasket.CompProperties_CoreSparks">
        <effecterDef>OLWC_CoreSparks</effecterDef>
        <onlyWhileDrafted>true</onlyWhileDrafted>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>OLWC_ResurrectMech</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
      <li>
        <compClass>OverlordWarcasket.CompDevResetCooldowns</compClass>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.CompProperties_ShieldBubble">
        <compClass>VEF.Apparels.CompShieldBubble</compClass>
        <blockRangedAttack>true</blockRangedAttack>
        <blockMeleeAttack>false</blockMeleeAttack>
        <showWhenDrafted>true</showWhenDrafted>
        <showOnHostiles>true</showOnHostiles>
        <showOnNeutralInCombat>true</showOnNeutralInCombat>
        <shieldTexPath>Other/ShieldBubble</shieldTexPath>
        <chargeFullyWhenMade>true</chargeFullyWhenMade>
        <minShieldSize>2.1</minShieldSize>
        <maxShieldSize>2.7</maxShieldSize>
        <disableRotation>true</disableRotation>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
        <traitsOnEquip>
          <li>OLWC_WarcasketTrait_Overlord</li>
        </traitsOnEquip>
        <traitsOnUnequip>
          <li>VFEP_Shellcasket</li>
        </traitsOnUnequip>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
